  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize capturing the **Ten of Diamonds** and the **Two of Clubs**. These cards count for points themselves and contribute to both the 'Most Cards' and 'Most Clubs' categories.\n\nThe 'Seven' Rule: Hold your middle-rank cards (5s, 6s, 7s). These are the most flexible for capturing combinations of low cards (Aces, 2s, 3s).\n\nLast-Round Denial: If you know the stock is empty, try to be the last person to capture ANY card. The person who makes the last capture gets all the remaining cards on the table for free.",
    Player: "Prioritize capturing the **Ten of Diamonds** and the **Two of Clubs**. These cards count for points themselves and contribute to both the 'Most Cards' and 'Most Clubs' categories.\n\nThe 'Seven' Rule: Hold your middle-rank cards (5s, 6s, 7s). These are the most flexible for capturing combinations of low cards (Aces, 2s, 3s).\n\nLast-Round Denial: If you know the stock is empty, try to be the last person to capture ANY card. The person who makes the last capture gets all the remaining cards on the table for free.",
